Unsupported gateway backup operations
====================================

OPNsense's reviewed core BackupController (26.7.4) provides inventory, download,
delete and revert operations. It does not provide the backup/backup action
previously used by FreeSDN to create a history entry. The adapter now returns
NOT_SUPPORTED without dispatching that operation; the direct client raises
CapabilityNotSupportedError, including when force=True was supplied. A forced
write cannot make an unsupported API exist. The standard gateway write mapper
returns HTTP 501 with a fixed explanation after normal access checks and
adapter connection succeed. No saved backup is claimed.

The OpenWrt adapter cannot enumerate device backup history. It now returns
NOT_SUPPORTED instead of manufacturing an empty successful list. The existing
inventory service maps that result to HTTP 501. In contrast, a successfully
retrieved empty OPNsense inventory remains a valid empty list.

Protected configuration exports remain separate and unchanged. OpenWrt's
create_backup adapter method remains the archive-export implementation used by
download_config; it does not establish managed storage, retention or restore
durability. Unifying that legacy method with the generic on-device creation UI
is still a separate capability-contract issue. The current UI may display a
creation action that receives an unsupported response; no per-operation UI
capability model is claimed by this backend correction.

Existing authentication, organization/site visibility, deletion checks and
write permissions are preserved. An unsupported operation does not bypass
those checks or turn an unauthorized request into an informative capability
response. The regression fixtures use actual adapters and PostgreSQL while
explicitly replacing authentication and device transport. They are not real
hardware backup or restore qualification.

Managed encrypted artifact storage, retention, restore validation and measured
recovery objectives remain outstanding. See also GATEWAY-BACKUP-TRIGGER,
GATEWAY-BACKUP-INVENTORY, GATEWAY-BACKUP-INVENTORY-UI and
OPNSENSE-BACKUP-MUTATIONS for the distinct backup boundaries.

